1
00:00:00,007 --> 00:00:01,216
[footsteps]

2
00:00:01,299 --> 00:00:03,427
INOMATA

3
00:00:06,471 --> 00:00:10,434
[Yukiko] Hey! You are on a roll, Chinatsu!
We're so proud!

4
00:00:11,018 --> 00:00:13,562
I am so, so happy for you!

5
00:00:14,604 --> 00:00:16,440
Count on me to cheer you on.

6
00:00:16,523 --> 00:00:18,900
We've got to have you strong
for nationals.

7
00:00:18,984 --> 00:00:21,737
- We'll have a feast tonight.
- [Chinatsu] Thank you so much.

8
00:00:21,820 --> 00:00:23,280
[emotional music playing]

9
00:00:23,363 --> 00:00:24,573
[Taiki] <i>That's great.</i>

10
00:00:26,199 --> 00:00:28,368
<i>Chinatsu made it through to nationals.</i>

11
00:00:29,327 --> 00:00:30,370
<i>That's great.</i>

12
00:00:31,246 --> 00:00:32,205
<i>That's great.</i>

13
00:00:33,457 --> 00:00:34,499
<i>Amazing.</i>

14
00:00:34,583 --> 00:00:35,959
<i>That's amazing!</i>

15
00:00:36,752 --> 00:00:39,713
<i>She said she would,
and she did it. That's...</i>

16
00:00:40,756 --> 00:00:41,923
<i>really cool.</i>

17
00:00:46,136 --> 00:00:47,220
<i>Even though...</i>

18
00:00:49,598 --> 00:00:50,599
[referee] In!

19
00:00:51,183 --> 00:00:52,267
Game.

20
00:00:52,350 --> 00:00:55,604
Twenty-one eleven, twenty-one thirteen.

21
00:00:55,687 --> 00:00:58,982
Yusa of Sajikawa High School wins.

22
00:01:03,695 --> 00:01:04,696
<i>Even though...</i>

23
00:01:05,489 --> 00:01:07,491
[runs, pants]

24
00:01:07,574 --> 00:01:08,742
<i>even though...</i>

25
00:01:12,329 --> 00:01:13,580
<i>even though...</i>

26
00:01:23,340 --> 00:01:24,508
<i>I lost.</i>

27
00:01:30,096 --> 00:01:32,098
[opening theme song playing]

28
00:01:33,183 --> 00:01:36,436
BLUE BOX

29
00:02:52,596 --> 00:02:58,977
BLUE BOX

30
00:02:59,561 --> 00:03:04,190
EPISODE 9
I'LL BE ROOTING FOR YOU

31
00:03:04,274 --> 00:03:05,984
[insects trilling]

32
00:03:06,067 --> 00:03:07,736
[kids laughing, running]

33
00:03:07,819 --> 00:03:08,904
[kid 1] Hurry up!

34
00:03:08,987 --> 00:03:09,988
[kid 2] Wait!

35
00:03:10,071 --> 00:03:11,448
[kid 1] Slow poke!

36
00:03:13,074 --> 00:03:15,243
OYASU SHRINE

37
00:03:22,208 --> 00:03:25,921
[school bell chimes]

38
00:03:34,596 --> 00:03:36,014
[Taiki] I have nothing left.

39
00:03:37,766 --> 00:03:39,059
I'm at my limit.

40
00:03:40,352 --> 00:03:42,520
There's nothing left to do but give up.

41
00:03:44,606 --> 00:03:46,399
Finals are gonna kill me!

42
00:03:47,609 --> 00:03:48,693
FINALS IN 7 DAYS

43
00:03:48,777 --> 00:03:51,529
Why do exams have to be
right after the tournament?

44
00:03:52,614 --> 00:03:55,075
That's why I said
study little by little, dude.

45
00:03:55,158 --> 00:03:56,409
Time for practice.

46
00:03:56,493 --> 00:03:58,286
Studying a little here and there

47
00:03:58,370 --> 00:04:00,705
is the hardest thing
to do in the whole world.

48
00:04:00,789 --> 00:04:02,832
You say it like it's so easy to do.

49
00:04:03,416 --> 00:04:05,752
[exclaims] You'll never understand me!

50
00:04:05,835 --> 00:04:07,420
You're really in your feels.

51
00:04:07,504 --> 00:04:10,423
[playing instruments]

52
00:04:14,261 --> 00:04:15,178
Hey there, girl!

53
00:04:15,262 --> 00:04:16,388
Hey, how's it going?

54
00:04:17,555 --> 00:04:19,683
Which category are you going for?

55
00:04:19,766 --> 00:04:21,601
I'm thinking recitation.

56
00:04:25,522 --> 00:04:27,524
MATHEMATICS

57
00:04:27,607 --> 00:04:29,943
[Taiki] We still have practice
during finals week.

58
00:04:30,568 --> 00:04:34,197
When I get home,
I don't have any energy left for studying.

59
00:04:34,281 --> 00:04:36,825
- You don't struggle finding time to train.
- [exclaims]

60
00:04:36,908 --> 00:04:37,993
{\an8}Hina!

61
00:04:41,663 --> 00:04:44,582
Could you do me a favor
and not talk to me?

62
00:04:45,875 --> 00:04:49,546
If it ain't Spanish, then I do not
have room in my brain for it right now.

63
00:04:50,171 --> 00:04:52,590
At long last, a friend who understands me.

64
00:04:53,675 --> 00:04:56,344
[Hina] Oh, no, we are not
in the same category.

65
00:04:56,428 --> 00:04:58,388
I've never gotten an F before!

66
00:04:58,471 --> 00:04:59,681
I haven't gotten one either!

67
00:04:59,764 --> 00:05:02,434
- [Hina] Second year of junior high.
- Dude, I had a stomachache!

68
00:05:02,517 --> 00:05:04,853
[Hina] Oh, uh-huh, whatever you say.

69
00:05:09,065 --> 00:05:09,899
[girl 1] Keep it up!

70
00:05:09,983 --> 00:05:11,901
{\an8}- [girl 2] Come on!
- [girl 3] Here!

71
00:05:11,985 --> 00:05:12,944
{\an8}[girl 2] Yeah!

72
00:05:13,028 --> 00:05:14,946
{\an8}Girls' basketball
is already back to practicing.

73
00:05:15,030 --> 00:05:16,156
{\an8}- Focus on your legwork!
- Yes!

74
00:05:16,239 --> 00:05:17,282
Focus!

75
00:05:17,365 --> 00:05:19,367
- Defense! Defense!
- Come on. Let's go!

76
00:05:19,451 --> 00:05:20,952
- Yes!
- You got this!

77
00:05:21,036 --> 00:05:23,663
There's only two months until nationals.

78
00:05:23,747 --> 00:05:25,874
They do extended practices at night, too.

79
00:05:25,957 --> 00:05:26,916
Yes!

80
00:05:30,462 --> 00:05:32,881
MATHEMATICS

81
00:05:32,964 --> 00:05:35,508
Well, we can't let them show us up!

82
00:05:35,592 --> 00:05:39,220
Okay, let's forget about studying
and practice, practice, practice!

83
00:05:41,973 --> 00:05:44,017
Taiki's on the struggle bus, huh?

84
00:05:45,351 --> 00:05:46,644
[Kyo sighs]

85
00:05:46,728 --> 00:05:49,230
[Hina] After he lost at qualifiers,

86
00:05:49,314 --> 00:05:53,651
he said something like, he expected it
to turn out that way, but still...

87
00:05:54,861 --> 00:05:57,572
And then of course
Chinatsu got into nationals, so...

88
00:05:58,281 --> 00:05:59,991
home life must be weird.

89
00:06:00,867 --> 00:06:02,202
Based on what I've heard,

90
00:06:02,285 --> 00:06:04,329
they haven't really talked much lately.

91
00:06:04,996 --> 00:06:07,165
With practice and exams going on.

92
00:06:09,000 --> 00:06:10,168
Gotcha.

93
00:06:11,920 --> 00:06:15,006
[Kyo] <i>She's not the type
to hear that and feel happy about it.</i>

94
00:06:16,966 --> 00:06:19,260
Taiki will be just fine, I'm sure.

95
00:06:19,803 --> 00:06:23,306
Immediately getting over stuff that's hard
for him is Taiki's strong suit.

96
00:06:26,851 --> 00:06:28,812
[Hina] When you're right, you're right!

97
00:06:30,188 --> 00:06:31,815
[Coach Yuasa] Well, then! Once again,

98
00:06:32,690 --> 00:06:33,775
Kengo Haryu,

99
00:06:34,442 --> 00:06:36,653
congrats on qualifying for nationals!

100
00:06:38,905 --> 00:06:40,865
It's a damn good thing, too.

101
00:06:40,949 --> 00:06:43,785
If Sajikawa nabbed all the spots,
that would grind my gears.

102
00:06:44,786 --> 00:06:45,829
[Haryu] That's all?

103
00:06:46,913 --> 00:06:49,332
I couldn't have done it without you all.

104
00:06:50,208 --> 00:06:53,837
And until nationals,
I might be a bit of a thorn in your side,

105
00:06:54,671 --> 00:06:57,340
but your support means everything.

106
00:07:02,429 --> 00:07:05,515
[chuckles] Bring it on, my man!

107
00:07:05,598 --> 00:07:06,766
I don't need your help.

108
00:07:06,850 --> 00:07:07,892
What!

109
00:07:07,976 --> 00:07:09,352
I said I'd help!

110
00:07:10,812 --> 00:07:12,897
You won't be playing doubles for a while.

111
00:07:13,398 --> 00:07:14,357
Guess you're right.

112
00:07:15,108 --> 00:07:18,820
Okay. Having said all that,
now that things have calmed down,

113
00:07:18,903 --> 00:07:21,865
I want each of you to write down
your goals and put 'em on the wall.

114
00:07:24,117 --> 00:07:25,493
Our goals, huh?

115
00:07:25,577 --> 00:07:26,911
What should we write down?

116
00:07:27,495 --> 00:07:29,873
I wanna shoot for something ambitious.

117
00:07:29,956 --> 00:07:32,167
{\an8}WITH FORTITUDE AND RESOLUTION
- KASAHARA

118
00:07:32,250 --> 00:07:34,377
{\an8}[Okayama] Uh, what does that mean?

119
00:07:35,962 --> 00:07:37,130
Strong and decisive.

120
00:07:37,213 --> 00:07:39,883
- All righty. I'm all done.
- Hm?

121
00:07:39,966 --> 00:07:42,635
- [giggles]
- Hold on a sec, Nishida.

122
00:07:42,719 --> 00:07:43,887
{\an8}MAKE NATIONALS!
- NISHIDA

123
00:07:43,970 --> 00:07:46,139
{\an8}If you made a mistake,
you should've started over.

124
00:07:46,222 --> 00:07:49,100
I put my feelings into it,
so the message carries!

125
00:07:49,184 --> 00:07:50,977
- [scoffs]
- [Nishida] Hm?

126
00:07:51,811 --> 00:07:53,396
What's yours, Haryu?

127
00:07:53,480 --> 00:07:57,108
WIN NATIONALS (THIS YEAR IF POSSIBLE)
- HARYU

128
00:07:57,192 --> 00:07:59,652
[Nishida] Could you not put that
right above mine, man?

129
00:08:00,653 --> 00:08:03,156
Yeah, we should put
Haryu's goal on the ceiling!

130
00:08:03,239 --> 00:08:05,825
What? Maybe putting it
on the ceiling would "seal" the deal!

131
00:08:05,909 --> 00:08:07,327
- Yeah.
- [both laugh]

132
00:08:09,037 --> 00:08:09,913
Done.

133
00:08:17,045 --> 00:08:18,713
[Tanikawa] Taiki, pass me the tape?

134
00:08:19,506 --> 00:08:20,673
Sure!

135
00:08:20,757 --> 00:08:22,425
{\an8}INCREASE MY SMASH PRECISION
- INOMATA

136
00:08:22,509 --> 00:08:26,262
{\an8}[Coach Yuasa] And you. Write on there that
you won't get any failing grades, huh?

137
00:08:26,346 --> 00:08:30,058
{\an8}[Nishida] Coach, I'm not gonna write
something down that I can't actually do.

138
00:08:30,141 --> 00:08:32,685
{\an8}- [chuckles]
- [Coach Yuasa] I swear, Nishida...

139
00:08:34,979 --> 00:08:35,897
[Taiki] Here.

140
00:08:35,980 --> 00:08:37,065
[Tanikawa] Thank you!

141
00:08:42,737 --> 00:08:48,034
[speaking accented Spanish]

142
00:08:54,290 --> 00:08:55,416
[player 1] You got it!

143
00:08:56,000 --> 00:08:57,460
[player 2] Let's go!

144
00:08:57,544 --> 00:09:00,213
- [player 3] <i>Vamos!</i>
- [player 4] This isn't Spanish class, man!

145
00:09:00,296 --> 00:09:02,298
[uplifting music playing]

146
00:09:05,885 --> 00:09:07,220
[Chinatsu pants]

147
00:09:07,303 --> 00:09:08,263
- Keep it up!
- Yes! Yeah!

148
00:09:19,566 --> 00:09:20,483
[sneezes]

149
00:09:22,902 --> 00:09:24,487
<i>Do I have a cold?</i>

150
00:09:26,030 --> 00:09:27,740
<i>Guess I should take a break.</i>

151
00:09:33,580 --> 00:09:36,249
[Yukiko] Oh, Chinatsu, welcome back.

152
00:09:37,333 --> 00:09:39,043
They keep you out late these days!

153
00:09:39,127 --> 00:09:41,421
I know, I'm really sorry about that.

154
00:09:41,504 --> 00:09:44,090
Oh, no! No sweat at all, it's fine!

155
00:09:44,173 --> 00:09:46,092
Don't worry yourself on our account.

156
00:09:46,175 --> 00:09:48,261
It's for nationals, after all.

157
00:09:48,344 --> 00:09:50,430
[Chinatsu] Thank you for understanding.

158
00:09:50,513 --> 00:09:53,391
TAIKI
CHINATSU

159
00:09:54,851 --> 00:09:56,811
[silence]

160
00:10:09,866 --> 00:10:11,618
[insects trilling]

161
00:10:15,872 --> 00:10:19,292
- [Nishida] <i>Finals week is over!</i>
- [all cheering]

162
00:10:19,375 --> 00:10:21,544
- Yes, yes!
- This about killed us all!

163
00:10:21,628 --> 00:10:23,796
- We made it through!
- Hm. Hm.

164
00:10:23,880 --> 00:10:26,799
Even after finals,
we didn't skip practice!

165
00:10:27,634 --> 00:10:28,760
No matter what,

166
00:10:28,843 --> 00:10:30,678
we made it through,
and that's what counts!

167
00:10:30,762 --> 00:10:32,305
[both] You heard him! That's right!

168
00:10:33,389 --> 00:10:35,183
Let's celebrate at a restaurant.

169
00:10:35,266 --> 00:10:36,476
Yeah, dude!

170
00:10:36,559 --> 00:10:39,187
- Nishida's paying, everybody!
- [exclaims]

171
00:10:39,270 --> 00:10:40,313
I'm there, man!

172
00:10:41,314 --> 00:10:43,107
[Nishida] Wait! Who decided that?

173
00:10:43,191 --> 00:10:45,151
Do you think you're gonna join them?

174
00:10:45,234 --> 00:10:49,072
[groans, trembles]
I'm gonna pass on this one.

175
00:10:49,155 --> 00:10:51,115
Whoa, are you okay, dude?

176
00:10:51,199 --> 00:10:55,078
I just got a bit short on sleep.
If I go rest at home, I'll be fine.

177
00:10:57,163 --> 00:11:00,583
I gotta come back
full-force to practice starting tomorrow!

178
00:11:01,793 --> 00:11:02,835
See you guys later!

179
00:11:02,919 --> 00:11:04,504
- See you, Taiki.
- See you later.

180
00:11:04,587 --> 00:11:05,546
[door closes]

181
00:11:05,630 --> 00:11:07,840
- It's about time we all headed out.
- Let's eat.

182
00:11:11,177 --> 00:11:13,346
INOMATA

183
00:11:16,307 --> 00:11:18,976
[footsteps]

184
00:11:23,439 --> 00:11:24,607
[groans]

185
00:11:26,526 --> 00:11:27,777
<i>My head hurts.</i>

186
00:11:29,654 --> 00:11:31,406
<i>I definitely have a fever.</i>

187
00:11:33,241 --> 00:11:34,659
<i>I want some Pocari.</i>

188
00:11:35,743 --> 00:11:37,495
<i>But no one's here to help me.</i>

189
00:11:38,704 --> 00:11:43,042
<i>And I cannot, under any circumstances,
get Chinatsu sick.</i>

190
00:11:44,293 --> 00:11:46,504
<i>Oh, this is bad.</i>

191
00:11:47,797 --> 00:11:48,965
[groans]

192
00:11:52,051 --> 00:11:53,636
<i>It's times like these...</i>

193
00:11:54,387 --> 00:11:56,055
[emotional music playing]

194
00:11:58,558 --> 00:12:00,393
<i>I remember the bad things.</i>

195
00:12:02,478 --> 00:12:05,815
<i>I was just starting to forget
about all that, thanks to exams.</i>

196
00:12:07,984 --> 00:12:11,696
<i>If I weren't sick,
I could go run and clear my head.</i>

197
00:12:14,490 --> 00:12:15,616
[coughs]

198
00:12:16,951 --> 00:12:18,578
[breathing heavily]

199
00:12:21,622 --> 00:12:23,666
You have to go to nationals.

200
00:12:25,251 --> 00:12:26,752
Thank you.

201
00:12:26,836 --> 00:12:28,045
Taiki Inomata.

202
00:12:30,965 --> 00:12:32,592
Don't be too careful with it.

203
00:12:33,301 --> 00:12:34,218
I'll win the next one.

204
00:12:35,261 --> 00:12:36,345
That's the spirit.

205
00:12:36,429 --> 00:12:37,472
But...

206
00:12:38,014 --> 00:12:39,765
I think he's gonna be a real force.

207
00:12:41,100 --> 00:12:42,435
Gotcha.

208
00:12:42,518 --> 00:12:44,437
Don't drive yourself crazy overthinking.

209
00:12:44,520 --> 00:12:46,272
You just gotta show 'em
what you're made of.

210
00:12:48,191 --> 00:12:54,822
<i>Please... please... I pray for both
Chinatsu and I to make it to nationals.</i>

211
00:12:56,324 --> 00:12:57,992
Then score... one more!

212
00:13:00,328 --> 00:13:01,412
[grunts]

213
00:13:07,251 --> 00:13:08,628
[exclaims]

214
00:13:16,552 --> 00:13:18,095
I'm a total loser.

215
00:13:20,515 --> 00:13:21,641
[Chinatsu] That's not true.

216
00:13:22,266 --> 00:13:23,809
[footsteps approaching]

217
00:13:27,355 --> 00:13:28,272
[Taiki gasps]

218
00:13:33,402 --> 00:13:34,779
You're burning up.

219
00:13:36,697 --> 00:13:37,657
[gasps]

220
00:13:41,244 --> 00:13:42,995
[Chinatsu] Is everything all right?

221
00:13:50,378 --> 00:13:51,546
[thuds]

222
00:13:52,296 --> 00:13:53,923
Hang on? Chinatsu?

223
00:13:54,006 --> 00:13:57,134
No, please, don't. You can't be in here.
I'm not feeling good.

224
00:13:57,218 --> 00:13:59,804
- It'd suck if you got it, so please--
- Can you stop already.

225
00:14:00,721 --> 00:14:02,807
If you're sick, then you should be quiet.

226
00:14:05,309 --> 00:14:06,227
Okay.

227
00:14:07,395 --> 00:14:09,021
[quirky music playing]

228
00:14:19,699 --> 00:14:22,618
COOLING PATCH

229
00:14:42,805 --> 00:14:45,391
- [knock on door]
- Uh. Come in.

230
00:14:49,061 --> 00:14:52,773
I thought that you should eat something,
and I found some udon noodles.

231
00:14:53,774 --> 00:14:54,650
Udon...

232
00:14:55,276 --> 00:14:57,486
<i>Did Chinatsu make me food?</i>

233
00:14:58,237 --> 00:14:59,780
- All right.
- [door closes]

234
00:15:02,158 --> 00:15:05,036
[Chinatsu] It sounds like
Yukiko is going to be back late.

235
00:15:05,828 --> 00:15:08,080
Sorry that the food is so simple.

236
00:15:10,124 --> 00:15:11,584
Thank you so much.

237
00:15:13,920 --> 00:15:16,088
<i>She made me a home-cooked meal.</i>

238
00:15:19,884 --> 00:15:21,093
Thanks for the food.

239
00:15:21,886 --> 00:15:23,471
[blowing]

240
00:15:30,478 --> 00:15:33,814
<i>My nose is so stuffed,
I can't even tell what it tastes like.</i>

241
00:15:34,857 --> 00:15:37,068
Just tell me
if there's anything else you need.

242
00:15:38,527 --> 00:15:39,737
I appreciate it.

243
00:15:42,448 --> 00:15:43,574
Hm?

244
00:15:45,618 --> 00:15:46,619
Nothing.

245
00:15:50,748 --> 00:15:53,209
<i>It's been a while
since we've been this close.</i>

246
00:15:53,292 --> 00:15:55,586
Two capsules is the dosage, right?

247
00:15:56,754 --> 00:15:57,588
{\an8}[Taiki] Um...

248
00:15:59,715 --> 00:16:03,594
I'm okay now, really.
You can head back to your room, Chinatsu.

249
00:16:04,470 --> 00:16:06,305
I'll stay here till you fall asleep.

250
00:16:06,806 --> 00:16:09,100
You never know,
you might start feeling a bit worse.

251
00:16:09,934 --> 00:16:12,103
I'm not feeling tired at all, though.

252
00:16:14,814 --> 00:16:17,358
Then, can we just talk for a little while?

253
00:16:17,984 --> 00:16:20,987
'Cause it's been chaotic
with all the tournaments and finals,

254
00:16:21,070 --> 00:16:22,613
we haven't really talked.

255
00:16:22,697 --> 00:16:25,366
And besides,
you mentioned a question the other day.

256
00:16:25,992 --> 00:16:27,994
You said there was something
you wanted to ask me

257
00:16:28,077 --> 00:16:29,704
once the tournament was over?

258
00:16:31,706 --> 00:16:33,374
Um, Chinatsu.

259
00:16:33,916 --> 00:16:36,627
After tomorrow,
could I ask you one question?

260
00:16:37,461 --> 00:16:40,047
Oh, did I say something like that?

261
00:16:40,131 --> 00:16:42,383
Don't play dumb with me, Taiki.

262
00:16:42,466 --> 00:16:45,219
[chuckles] Oh, no, I'm not playing dumb.

263
00:16:45,302 --> 00:16:46,262
[sniffles]

264
00:16:47,346 --> 00:16:48,639
<i>It's just that...</i>

265
00:16:50,349 --> 00:16:53,477
<i>I had the confidence then, to ask her.</i>

266
00:16:55,104 --> 00:16:58,441
[Chinatsu] Seeing Hina...
it made me jealous.

267
00:17:09,243 --> 00:17:11,912
Okay, then can I ask you a question?

268
00:17:12,830 --> 00:17:13,873
Yeah.

269
00:17:14,999 --> 00:17:18,919
{\an8}[Chinatsu] <i>I saw that the badminton team
put up their goal sheets today.</i>

270
00:17:19,003 --> 00:17:20,171
[Taiki gasps]

271
00:17:20,796 --> 00:17:22,214
And knowing you,

272
00:17:22,298 --> 00:17:24,967
I thought that your goal
would be going to nationals.

273
00:17:25,051 --> 00:17:26,677
[gentle music playing]

274
00:17:27,261 --> 00:17:28,679
So I want to know

275
00:17:28,763 --> 00:17:31,182
why is it that you wrote
something different?

276
00:17:32,767 --> 00:17:33,976
It's because...

277
00:17:35,144 --> 00:17:38,689
I've gone over it so many times
in my head about that smash...

278
00:17:38,773 --> 00:17:40,191
What if it had been in?

279
00:17:41,358 --> 00:17:45,946
I've also felt like the nationals
might've been setting my sights too high.

280
00:17:47,281 --> 00:17:49,450
<i>Once I made it to the tournament,</i>

281
00:17:49,533 --> 00:17:52,161
<i>there were so many people
way better than me.</i>

282
00:17:54,163 --> 00:17:55,581
You know what it's like.

283
00:17:55,664 --> 00:17:58,334
How tough it is
to make nationals as a first year.

284
00:17:58,417 --> 00:18:01,253
And in spite of that,
you still had determination.

285
00:18:02,755 --> 00:18:05,007
I just wanted it. I...

286
00:18:05,633 --> 00:18:07,134
wanted to go and win.

287
00:18:07,760 --> 00:18:10,012
So I thought maybe I was out of my depth.

288
00:18:12,598 --> 00:18:13,933
[chuckles]

289
00:18:15,559 --> 00:18:16,727
Wait, what?

290
00:18:16,811 --> 00:18:19,105
Are you laughing at me?

291
00:18:19,188 --> 00:18:20,231
I'm sorry.

292
00:18:21,857 --> 00:18:24,985
So even the great Taiki
sometimes doubts himself.

293
00:18:26,695 --> 00:18:28,072
Oh, thank you for the food.

294
00:18:28,614 --> 00:18:29,990
I hope you liked it.

295
00:18:30,616 --> 00:18:33,911
I mean, I figured
you might think those things...

296
00:18:33,994 --> 00:18:36,497
but I thought you were the type
who'd never let on about it.

297
00:18:37,164 --> 00:18:38,541
Well, it's actually...

298
00:18:39,625 --> 00:18:42,753
This is your chance.
Why not reinvent yourself?

299
00:18:42,837 --> 00:18:43,838
[exclaims softly]

300
00:18:44,672 --> 00:18:46,590
You can still set an ambitious goal,

301
00:18:46,674 --> 00:18:48,467
and keep checking in with yourself.

302
00:18:50,177 --> 00:18:54,014
[Taiki] <i>But right now,
that ambitious goal is...</i>

303
00:18:55,057 --> 00:18:57,518
[Chinatsu] You said
that I am always determined...

304
00:18:59,478 --> 00:19:01,522
<i>but in the back of my mind,</i>

305
00:19:02,898 --> 00:19:04,525
<i>I'm also wondering...</i>

306
00:19:05,401 --> 00:19:08,779
<i>"Am I aiming too high?
Is this impossible?"</i>

307
00:19:09,613 --> 00:19:12,032
<i>Sometimes, all I would feel is pressure...</i>

308
00:19:12,116 --> 00:19:13,409
[laughs]

309
00:19:17,872 --> 00:19:20,791
and I'd ask myself,
"Why don't I just ease up?"

310
00:19:22,835 --> 00:19:25,796
But then I would
hate myself for thinking that.

311
00:19:27,423 --> 00:19:28,299
That said,

312
00:19:29,383 --> 00:19:31,927
what got me out of bed early
every morning...

313
00:19:32,636 --> 00:19:34,305
was wanting to go to nationals.

314
00:19:35,514 --> 00:19:37,474
If there's something that you wanna do,

315
00:19:37,558 --> 00:19:39,310
or something you wanna be,

316
00:19:39,393 --> 00:19:41,437
I want you to feel good about that.

317
00:19:42,563 --> 00:19:46,317
I don't want you to be afraid
to set your sights on something big.

318
00:19:47,151 --> 00:19:48,819
No matter how big it might be.

319
00:19:49,403 --> 00:19:52,072
If that goal motivates you to keep going,

320
00:19:52,156 --> 00:19:54,325
then I believe that's good enough.

321
00:19:55,534 --> 00:19:57,203
And it's those people

322
00:19:57,286 --> 00:19:58,829
I wanna root for.

323
00:19:59,955 --> 00:20:01,165
[gasps]

324
00:20:01,957 --> 00:20:03,334
[coughs]

325
00:20:05,294 --> 00:20:07,546
- Are you okay?
- Yeah.

326
00:20:08,422 --> 00:20:10,591
Sorry. You should get some rest.

327
00:20:11,800 --> 00:20:14,094
[Taiki sighs] <i>I...</i>

328
00:20:16,013 --> 00:20:18,390
<i>really like this side of her.</i>

329
00:20:19,433 --> 00:20:22,353
<i>She's had these feelings and doubts...</i>

330
00:20:22,436 --> 00:20:24,939
<i>but has worked through
all of them on her own.</i>

331
00:20:26,482 --> 00:20:28,609
<i>So she's an empathetic,</i>

332
00:20:30,736 --> 00:20:31,987
<i>and kind soul.</i>

333
00:20:34,823 --> 00:20:37,952
I'm going to add onto my goal sheet.

334
00:20:44,375 --> 00:20:45,626
All right.

335
00:20:52,341 --> 00:20:54,802
Well then, I'll get this out of the way.

336
00:20:55,386 --> 00:20:56,679
No, I can do it.

337
00:20:56,762 --> 00:20:58,389
It's fine! You just sleep.

338
00:20:59,014 --> 00:20:59,890
[Taiki] But...

339
00:21:07,648 --> 00:21:08,857
[thudding]

340
00:21:26,750 --> 00:21:28,210
[Taiki] I'm sorry.

341
00:21:30,045 --> 00:21:31,046
[gasps]

342
00:21:32,214 --> 00:21:34,425
I got up and lost my balance.

343
00:21:37,928 --> 00:21:38,929
Huh?

344
00:22:05,581 --> 00:22:07,583
[closing theme song playing]
